    "wacc_rationale": "USD flows, USD rate. Cost of equity ~8.5% (US 10y ~4.25% + beta ~0.8 x 5.0% ERP + small leverage premium); after-tax cost of debt ~4.0% (FY2025 interest incurred $7.0B on ~$135B book debt = 5.2% pre-tax, 22% tax). Market-value weights ~52% equity ($169B) / 48% debt+NCI ($157B pro forma) give ~6.3%; rounded UP to 7.0% because the debt stack reprices upward as ~$9B/yr matures and the EchoStar deal lifts leverage to ~3x. Same WACC in all three scenarios: risk is carried in the driver paths and weights, not a per-scenario premium.",
    "lease_treatment": "US GAAP ASC 842: operating-lease cost sits inside EBITDA and OCF, so leases are in the flows; operating lease liabilities ($22.5B FY2025) are therefore NOT in net debt. Finance leases ($1.4B) are inside book debt. One treatment, applied once.",
    "nci_treatment": "Flows are 100% consolidated, so the $15,990M noncontrolling interest (Jun-2026 balance sheet; mostly Telco LLC preferred interests carrying ~$1.4B/yr of distributions) is deducted at book in the equity bridge. Charged once.",
    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF DCF (component route), 10-year horizon. AT&T is a pure-play US connectivity operating company after the 2022 WarnerMedia spin and DIRECTV exit - not a bank, REIT or holdco - so the routing table sends it to owner-FCF; no prior DCF and no memory entry exist, so this is a fresh build. Mid-cycle normalisation: the explicit years carry the guided $23-24B capital investment (capex + vendor-financing payments, ~18% of revenue, above the 16.6% cash-capex line in the CSV because AT&T's FCF definition also deducts vendor-financing payments) through the fiber build to 60M passings by 2030, then fade network capex to ~15%. SPECTRUM: spectrum purchases sit outside capex but are a recurring owner cost (AWS-3 2015, C-band 2021, 3.45GHz 2022, EchoStar $23B 2026 = ~$6B/yr average over a decade); the EchoStar payment (closed 2026-07-28) is deducted in the bridge and a normalised spectrum charge of 1.0-1.5pp of revenue (base), 0.5-1.0pp (bull), 2.0-2.5pp (bear) is folded into capex_pct_path from 2029 (upper C-band auction). DEBT: Metrics.csv TotalDebt (143,954 at Q2-26) double-counts the current portion - XBRL LongTermDebt (134,718 at FY2025) already includes debt maturing within one year and ties to face 144,311 less 9,193 unamortised discount; total debt used = 143,954 - 9,323 = 134,631. CASH TAX: FY2025 cash tax $1.35B and H1-26 $91M reflect OBBBA 100% bonus depreciation on a capex-heavy base; ramped 3% -> 22% (21% federal + net state) by FY2033. Year-1 build gives ~$22B unlevered owner FCF; less ~$7.5B after-tax-ish interest that is ~$15-16B levered vs the $18B+ guide - the ~$2B gap is device-receivable/working-capital timing that is not projected as recurring (conservative). Buybacks: active repurchaser ($4.5B FY2025, $4.7B H1-26, ~$10B 2026 target) so the flat count is genuinely funded.",
